  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've just installed a shiny new easy grip faucet, only to find it's dripping or leaking. One common culprit is a misseated O-ring. That little rubber ring is essential for creating a watertight seal, so make sure it's snugly in place when you're positioning the faucet through the sink hole. Another frequent error is not tightening the mounting nut enough – or, on the flip side, overtightening it! You want it secure, but not so tight you strip the threads or crack something. Sometimes, the supply-line connector might not be the right fit for your home's plumbing, leading to drips there. Always double-check those connections before you even think about turning the water back on. And don't forget the plumber's tape if your instructions call for it! If you've gone through all these checks and the leak persists, or if you're dealing with really tight access under the sink, that's a good sign it might be time to call in a professional. They've got the tools and expertise to diagnose and fix those tricky leaks quickly. HH Remodeling LLC here in Aurora, serving the greater Denver area, can certainly help if you're facing persistent plumbing issues.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
